	(text "R1 converts SiPM \ncurrent pulse \nto voltage\n\n--Why 49.9--\ntradeoff: bigger R => \nbigger V \nbut slower recovery \ntime from \nSiPM's capacitors. \nMuon is\nrare enough that\nwe don't need\nfast recovery time."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 60.706 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0afc16b0-100d-4314-a19e-cdfad235aa97")
	)
	(text "J1 is the cable \nconnector to Grant's \npower/interface board.\n------------\nPin 1,3,5 brings\npower in. Pin 7 \nsends TRIG \nout to the FPGA\n------------\nEvery signal is paired \nwith an adjacent GRND so \nits return current \nhas a short path right \nbeside it. That keeps \nthe loop area small, \nwhich limits both what \nthe cable radiates \nand what it picks up.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.858 145.542 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "13b49b95-37d2-4c2a-a62b-e8e8b5a1b6ab")
	)
	(text "cable has its\nown impedance.\nR7 smooths out\noverall V output\n---------\nThe target is R7 + \ncomparator output \nimpedance ≈ cable \nimpedance"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 262.128 61.214 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2c00c6cd-74ce-4c62-9f37-801f5699258e")
	)
	(text "Voltage-divider circuit:\nV_out \n= V_in × R4/(R3+R4)\n= 0.050 V.\nso, V_out going into \nU1B's + pin is 50 mV "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 85.598 68.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "433f6707-04d0-464c-938e-64b831eba725")
	)
	(text "U2: VOLTAGE-COMPARATOR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.126 36.322 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "693c3eb1-a4fd-4ea5-aa9e-9264b6fc1ba2")
	)
	(text "R5 combined with \nstray C at the − input \ncan cause ringing \nif it's too large."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.42 28.956 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6d4021a4-d41e-46dd-9680-6f63121a5c27")
	)
	(text "Why R2=499 ohms:\n1) low thermal noise V = √(4kTRB)\ngoing into U1A's + pin.\n2) balanced high-pass filter.\n3) op-amp pushes small current\nout the + pin, high R means high\nunwanted V.\nNot magic #(300 or 1k would also work)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.888 54.356 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6d9f9bcf-aea6-4440-8837-264ec6df5af2")
	)
	(text "U1C dictates max\n& min of U1A output\n---------------\nWe want 5V to\nleave room for\nmassive high V\nevents coming\nfrom the SiPM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 138.43 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "83ea87eb-6885-4f8d-a81b-cf41f019d4d2")
	)
	(text "U1B's job is to produce\na constant tiny voltage\nVBASE (50 mV) that U1A\nuses as baseline.\n\nU1A can't use 0 as baseline\nbecause the AC coupling \nfrom C1 forces a 0 average\nvoltage so positive pulses\nwill result in negative\npulses afterwards, and when\nnegative vultages are fed\ninto op-amps, they need\ntime to recover & ruin\nsignal integrity.\n\nWe're using a voltage divider\nto get that tiny voltage,\nbut it's output fluctuates\nwith load & comes with high-\nimpedance, so we feed it into\nU1B to steady it and get rid of\nimpedance.\n-------------------\nVBASE = 50 mV = V_out\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 86.106 103.378 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "85679b90-a364-48ad-9880-eafcf84d5e27")
	)
	(text "RV1: potentiometer\nBelow V_set, \noutput\nis 0V; above, \noutput\nis 3.3 V\n---------\nset at ~100 mV"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.726 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "942cda0a-7f91-4e33-b6a1-0dfd27460371")
	)
	(text "Decoupling C: \nConnected in \nparallel between \nthe power pins \nand ground (near \nan IC) to stabilize\nvoltage and \nshunt high-freq\nnoise\n--------\nWhy two values per \nrail: a real C stops \nbehaving like a C \nabove its self-resonant freq, \nwhere its own package \ninductance takes over. \n--------\nThe 100n is small and fast - good at high freq. \nThe 10u holds more charge but is slower - \ngood for larger, slower load changes.\nTogether they cover a wider band than either alone.\n--------\nThe rule is: capacitor as close \nto the IC's supply pins \nas you can physically place \nit, ideally a few millimeters, \nwith a short path to ground."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.968 140.462 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ce07b5ba-3930-4c13-bedc-edf284d91ce1")
	)
	(text "C1-R2 is high pass filter\nin 1/(2πRC) ≈ 3.2 kHz range. \nMuon detection is MHz range. \nRough rule: a signal \nwith rise time τ gives 0.35/τ \nfrequency.For muon detection \nwith 100 ns pulse that's ~3.5 MHz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90.424 30.226 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e81633ca-4580-4bd3-b21c-585735245f47")
	)
	(text "U1 contains 2 independent\nhigh-gain op-amps\n------------------\nGain = 1 + R5/R6 = 13.4\n------------------\nGain-bandwidth product (GBW)\nis a number that captures an \nop-amp's speed limit, it stays\nconstant. For TPH2502, \nGBW ~ 120 MHz,\nso at 13.4 gain => usable up\nto 120/13.4 ~ 9 mHz.\n------------------\n9 MHz is within the\nrough 3x-5x headroom\nguideline for the\nsignal we want to\namplify (~3.5 mHz, see C1) \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.452 74.422 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ec411f49-a3b1-4f41-93a9-aaae1345469d")
	)
	(text "C1/R2: AC coupling, \n~3.2 kHz corner"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 83.058 50.038 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f773eab6-7c1d-46b6-a1e2-aa4a1771dbb4")
	)
	(text "U2C dictates max\nand min of U2A output\n--------------\nWe want 3.3V\nbecause the FPGA\nprocessing the signals\ncan only do up to 3.3V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 258.572 89.916 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f7d5d306-db93-498f-b5ce-d81760e46726")
	)
